  "text": "{\"title\": \"Risks and open questions\", \"text\": \"The main risks include the proposal exceeding 15 pages or email transmission being delayed past 17:00 GMT on 2027-02-12, resulting in immediate rejection [RSK-001]. We would enforce a strict 12-page limit on the draft and test email submission with a dummy document one day prior [RSK-001]. A third-party monitoring or diagnostic tool exporting personal data outside the UK risks contract termination and regulatory penalties, so we would audit all third-party dependencies and logging destinations and pin all cloud resources to UK-based regions only [RSK-002]. Delays in core record deployment pushing back historic migration and staff training beyond 2027-06-30 risk missing the go-live deadline, which we would address by adding engineering resources to parallelize migration scripts and de-scoping non-essential historic records for post-go-live migration [RSK-003]. Open questions are whether the 99% availability requirement in REQ-0010 excludes scheduled maintenance windows [Q-01], and whether the existing donor spreadsheet mentioned in REQ-0007 can be accessed via automated scripts or requires manual intervention [Q-02].\", \"cited_ids\": [\"RSK-001\", \"RSK-002\", \"RSK-003\", \"Q-01\", \"Q-02\"]}",
